@meta
id: 19-12
title: A list of your own
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: location-list
par: 86
minutes: 6
vscode: nothing; the search panel is global
vimrc: set hidden
open: README.md

@brief
Every quickfix command so far has an `l` twin. `:lvimgrep` searches the
same way as `:vimgrep` and puts the results in the location list
instead. `:lopen` shows it, `:lne` and `:lp` step through it, `:ldo`
runs a command on every entry. The difference is ownership. There is
one quickfix list for the whole of vim. A location list belongs to a
window: each window can have its own, and a search in one window never
disturbs another's.

The job: four `: any` types under `src` become `: unknown`. Do it
through the location list. The two comments that disable the
`no-explicit-any` lint rule are not types and stay; they are also not
matched by a pattern that asks for `: any` as a whole word.

@keys
| `:lvimgrep` `:lvim` | search into this window's location list |
| `:lopen` `:lclose` | show and hide it |
| `:lne` `:lp` `:lfirst` `:llast` `:ll N` | step through it |
| `:ldo` `:lfdo` | run a command per entry, per file |

@hints
`:lvimgrep /: any\>/ **/*.ts`, then `:lopen` to see the four.
--
`:ldo s/: any\>/: unknown/g | update`. The same shape as `:cdo`, one
letter different.
--
`:qa`, because the location window is still open.

@solution
    :lvimgrep /: any\>/ **/*.ts<Enter>  :lopen<Enter>  :ldo s/: any\>/: unknown/g | update<Enter>  :qa<Enter>

Everything you know about the quickfix list transfers by changing the
first letter. What does not transfer is the scope. Split the window and
the new window gets a copy of the location list; close the window and
its list goes with it. The quickfix list outlives all of that.

The rule of thumb: the quickfix list for the job that spans the
session, the rename you are working through or the build you are
fixing; a location list for the question you are asking right now, in
this window, that you do not want to cost you the quickfix list. The
next lesson is that situation. Plugins follow the same split: a linter
that reports per file writes to the location list, a project-wide
search writes to quickfix.

The `\>` on the pattern is a word boundary. `: any` alone would also
match `: anything` if a type of that name existed. Cheap insurance.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: any, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
  public async cancelOrder(_: any, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@start src/domain/payment/payment.producer.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { Channel } from '../../infrastructure/rabbit/channel';

type RefundIssuedEvent = {
  paymentId: string;
  receipt: string;
};

@injectable()
export class PaymentProducer {
  constructor(@inject(Channel) protected channel: Channel) {}

  public async refundIssued(event: any) {
    await this.channel.publish('payments', 'payment.sendRefund', event);
  }
}

@expected src/domain/payment/payment.producer.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { Channel } from '../../infrastructure/rabbit/channel';

type RefundIssuedEvent = {
  paymentId: string;
  receipt: string;
};

@injectable()
export class PaymentProducer {
  constructor(@inject(Channel) protected channel: Channel) {}

  public async refundIssued(event: unknown) {
    await this.channel.publish('payments', 'payment.sendRefund', event);
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async sendRefund(orderId: string) {
    // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
    const response: any = await this.http.post('/sendRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async sendRefund(orderId: string) {
    // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
    const response: unknown = await this.http.post('/sendRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
